---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sectors, STRICT } from '../lib/content';
import { fmtDate, href } from '../lib/url';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
const tabs = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who made it' },
  { id: 'facts', label: 'How facts are sourced' },
  { id: 'ai', label: 'Use of AI' },
  { id: 'open', label: 'Open source and access' },
];
---
<Base title="About">
  <div class="container page">
    <h1>About the {SITE_NAME}</h1>
    <div class="cats" role="tablist" aria-label="About" data-switch>
      {tabs.map((t, i) => <button role="tab" id={`tab-${t.id}`} aria-controls={`panel-${t.id}`} aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}>{t.label}</button>)}
    </div>
    <div class="prose panels">
      <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-who" aria-labelledby="tab-who">
        <p>A student team in the Policy Innovation Lab at Carnegie Mellon University's Heinz College (Fall 2026), working with the Bloomberg Center for Government Excellence (GovEx) at Johns Hopkins. It is a prototype, not an official GovEx or Johns Hopkins product.</p>
      </section>
      <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-facts" aria-labelledby="tab-facts" hidden>
        <ul>
          <li>Every fact comes from the team's sector research and links to the public source it rests on, with an "as of" date.</li>
          <li>Items still waiting for a linked source show "Source pending". Claims still being checked show "Fact-check pending". Both are hidden in the version tested with officials.</li>
          <li>Map locations marked "approximate" are city centers, or a state or national capital for statewide and national entries.</li>
          <li>Likelihood and severity are the research team's judgment for a city with active deployments over the next few years, not statistical estimates.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Cases, rules and toolkit tools tagged "Pending team review" were found through web research by Claude Code to cover more places outside the US and what cities already do. Each has its sources; the team has not checked them yet.</p>
        <p class="small muted">This build: {STRICT ? 'strict mode (unsourced items hidden)' : 'draft mode (unsourced items shown and labeled)'}. Research snapshots: {sectors.map((s) => `${s.id} ${fmtDate(s.as_of)}`).join('; ')}.</p>
      </section>
      <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-ai" aria-labelledby="tab-ai" hidden>
        <p>Following our course's AI policy, we cite AI use. Claude (Anthropic) helped draft parts of the sector research, which the team checked and linked to sources. Claude Code helped write this site's code, convert the research documents into structured data, and adapt the illustrative 3D world. The 3D scenes are schematic, not engineering models.</p>
      </section>
      <section role="tabpanel" id="panel-open" aria-labelledby="tab-open" hidden>
        <p>The code is released under the Apache License 2.0. Map data from OpenStreetMap contributors, served by OpenFreeMap; offline outlines from Natural Earth. The low-poly 3D world on each Overview is Vyomesh Iyengar's design from his MVP (vyomesh-mvp in this repository), adapted to this site. Maps drawn with MapLibre GL. Fonts are Source Serif 4 and Work Sans (SIL Open Font License).</p>
        <p>We aim for WCAG 2.2 AA. Every diagram works from the keyboard, the 3D story has a text version, and the "Reduce motion" switch in the header turns off animation and page slides.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .panels { margin-top: var(--sp-5); min-height: 12rem; font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
  .panels li + li { margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
</style>
